-- For an odd prime p = 2h + 1, some multiple m p with 0 < m < p is
-- a² + b² + 1: the h + 1 residues x² and the h + 1 residues −1 − y² for
-- x, y ≤ h cannot all be distinct among p residues.
-- Part of the Arithmetic blueprint.
-- Planned home: NumberTheory/FourSquaresModPrime.
-- Copyright (c) 2026 Grant Passmore.
